Z||000000||Cooter||08-27-2000||06:21 PM||||I am tired of the POS modem in my new computer. I cant do anything without getting booted. It is not a wiring problem because my wifes computer is connected right beside mine and it performs perfectly. The only problem is my new M/B is a PCI only- and I dont really like PCI modems because they are software controlled. <BR>Anyway- I need a good PCI modem. Any good ones?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fearless Freep||08-27-2000||06:42 PM||||You dont expect anything less than the best for our cars....stick with the best modems.....just get a US Robotics....externals are nice because you can just reset it without turning the computer off.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fearless Freep||08-27-2000||06:45 PM||||Forgot to add one thing....I dont have a USR but Im running a Diamond Shotgun modem.  (2 modems in one.) when I want a little increase in bandwidth, I dial out with the second modem and multilink them together. On a good day I usually surf in the 93's.  Course the ISP has to support that technology.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
